      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DEBBIE LINCOLN NZ (6) has returned in terrific order, leading to win her two starts at this circuit and distance since a spell. Draws wider but has the gate speed to offset that and has won when third-up before so should be at her peak. Can continue on her winning way. ISLA ROCHELLE (2) has been kept fresh since she came from this barrier and battled on well for a 2m second to Debbie Lincoln six weeks ago. That continued a run of consistent form and she came from wider to win here four back. Could make a race of it. HARPERVILLE (4) produced a better effort last time out when runner-up at this circuit and distance. Can go well again. Looks a gap to the others, RACANA NZ (7) may be next best.",
